lientTest.java"],"commit":"393e7298630fda99fa2d770b868d78ef252ecf2c","parent":"2dfb6c22f2446cfc7380c9ecd6d48e42f7203a89","patch_sha256":"e5f6961f50f41b51d618cc3fe2276ba49fd4a58c6aac3eef8fc6fb04d8e9e446","subject":"Make Lettuce server-error tests independent of execution order","tree":"7a241c775c584cd007e389de7af0e44b8c3abf07"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"e5f6961f50f41b51d618cc3fe2276ba49fd4a58c6aac3eef8fc6fb04d8e9e446","finding_commits":{"inline:4329256347":"393e7298630fda99fa2d770b868d78ef252ecf2c","inline:4329256452":"393e7298630fda99fa2d770b868d78ef252ecf2c","review:5590421039":"393e7298630fda99fa2d770b868d78ef252ecf2c"},"parent":"2dfb6c22f2446cfc7380c9ecd6d48e42f7203a89","patch_sha256":"e5f6961f50f41b51d618cc3fe2276ba49fd4a58c6aac3eef8fc6fb04d8e9e446","tree":"7a241c775c584cd007e389de7af0e44b8c3abf07"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"The overview summarizes the two concrete TESTHM fixture dependencies reported inline. Both are fixed in commit 1 by initializing the existing hash map inside the WRONGTYPE tests, waiting for its single command trace, and clearing setup telemetry before GET. The existing cross-version getter suites passed (42 Lettuce 4 tests and 55 Lettuce 5 tests); Redis-backed installed-agent execution was not run because this launch does not support Docker-in-Docker. The overview identifies no additional concrete defect beyond its two linked issues.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5590421039"},{"analysis":"Confirmed: the frozen Lettuce 4 setUp initializes only TESTKEY, while TESTHM was created by testHashSetAndThenNestApplyToHashGetall. The error test now synchronously HMSETs TESTHM using TEST_HASH_MAP, waits for the HMSET trace, and clears captured telemetry before the failing GET. It no longer depends on test ordering, and reusing the identical map preserves the hash-content assertion in the other test.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4329256347"},{"analysis":"Confirmed: the frozen Lettuce 5 setUp initializes only TESTKEY, while TESTHM was created by testHashSetAndThenNestApplyToHashGetall. The error test now synchronously HMSETs TESTHM using testHashMap, waits for the HMSET trace, and clears captured telemetry before the failing GET. It no longer depends on test ordering, and reusing the identical map preserves the hash-content assertion in the other test.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4329256452"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"9fb09b84d39937719188063460389bce8f92e12b05ef94babf9162904a9dffa2","schema":2},"download_sha256":"4ac35bc71cb79e1a8616b5b071f086342e179cb32bda185982fa42e7f339fb77","frozen_sha":"2dfb6c22f2446cfc7380c9ecd6d48e42f7203a89","pr":20778,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"9fb09b84d39937719188063460389bce8f92e12b05ef94babf9162904a9dffa2","request_id":"3ee8dc50c1eb4bd0b083d0b6860ecaa4","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39485049366,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:4ac35bc71cb79e1a8616b5b071f086342e179cb32bda185982fa42e7f339fb77","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39488267795},"workflow_revision":"702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5590421039],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nCross-version error handling still needs human validation, and the integration tests have unresolved fixture dependencies.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>2 open issues</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Initialize TESTHM in setUp to avoid order-dependent WRONGTYPE test](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20778#discussion_r4329256347) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Initialize TESTHM in setUp to avoid order-dependent WRONGTYPE test](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20778#discussion_r4329256452) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nAdds Redis server-error classification to Lettuce 4.0 and 5.0 command and batch telemetry while preserving exception-class fallback for client failures.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Extracts validated Redis error prefixes.\n- Connects classification to command and batch attributes.\n- Adds getter tests and span/duration-metric assertions.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-5.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bunitTests/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv5_0/\u200bLettuceAttributesGetterTest.java | Tests classification and fallback. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-5.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200btest/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv5_0/\u200bLettuceAsyncClientTest.java | Checks command and batch error telemetry. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-5.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv5_0/\u200bLettuceRedisErrorType.java | Extracts validated error prefixes. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-5.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv5_0/\u200bLettuceDbAttributesGetter.java | Classifies command errors. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-5.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv5_0/\u200bLettuceBatchAttributesGetter.java | Classifies batch errors. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-4.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200btest/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv4_0/\u200bLettuceAsyncClientTest.java | Checks command and batch error telemetry. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-4.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv4_0/\u200bLettuceRedisErrorType.java | Extracts validated error prefixes. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-4.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv4_0/\u200bLettuceDbAttributesGetter.java | Classifies command errors. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-4.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv4_0/\u200bLettuceBatchAttributesGetter.java | Classifies batch errors. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200blettuce-4.0/\u200bjavaagent-unit-tests/\u200bsrc/\u200btest/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200blettuce/\u200bv4_0/\u200bLettuceDbAttributesGetterTest.java | Tests classification and fallback. |\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5590421039","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5590421039},{"body":"[Testing] `setUp()` creates only `TESTKEY`; `TESTHM` is populated by `testHashSetAndThenNestApplyToHashGetall`. Running this test alone, or before that test, makes GET return null instead of WRONGTYPE. Initialize the hash here using the existing fixture map, then drain and clear its telemetry before exercising the error. Reusing the map avoids adding fields that would change the other test's expected hash contents.","comment_commit_id":"2dfb6c22f2446cfc7380c9ecd6d48e42f7203a89","comment_id":4329256347,"key":"inline:4329256347","kind":"inline","line":194,"original_commit_id":"2dfb6c22f2446cfc7380c9ecd6d48e42f7203a89","original_line":194,"path":"instrumentation/lettuce/lettuce-4.0/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/lettuce/v4_0/LettuceAsyncClientTest.java","review_commit_id":"2dfb6c22f2446cfc7380c9ecd6d48e42f7203a89","review_id":5590421039,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-20T19:21:04Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"a78322ef926bdd0042c1613878ccbd2c4fc8943634119206b2a445107c69f9e8","id":4329256347,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-20T19:21:04Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86ufHxG"},{"body":"[Testing] `setUp()` creates only `TESTKEY`; `TESTHM` is populated by `testHashSetAndThenNestApplyToHashGetall`. Running this test alone, or before that test, makes GET return null instead of WRONGTYPE. Initialize the hash here using the 